Reason: every instance created or destroyed rebuilt the draw list and sorted all of it, tiles included. A GMS1 room
keeps its tiles in the list (rm_a5h04: about 2,300 entries with a few hundred instances), and AM2R creates and
destroys bubbles, sparks and debris most frames, so the water room spent about 7.5% of its CPU time in that sort
(Dolphin perf). The tile run from the previous rebuild is now reused when it still holds every tile once and is still
sorted at the current tile depths; only instances and particle systems are sorted, and the two sorted runs are merged.
The order is a strict total order (depth, type, then a unique index per type), so the merge gives the same list as one
full sort.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

--- a/src/runner.c
+++ b/src/runner.c
@@ -813,11 +813,64 @@
